  "notes": [
    "Batool ToUnicode maps CID to PUA (U+F0xx), not Arabic.",
    "Codes are in RTL reading order: rightmost glyph first.",
    "One code is one drawn shape. Different shapes of the same letter (initial/medial/final) get different codes.",
    "Ligatures map to more than one Unicode letter (example: F09F = لا).",
    "The decoder attaches combining marks (ِ ُ ً ّ ٓ ٰ) to the nearest host letter by x.",
    "Word spaces come from x-gaps between letters, not from a space glyph.",
    "F0F1+F031 is ائے (آبلائے). If an alef already sits before that pair, emit ئے only.",
    "F060 is ہ, except ن+F060+ی → ھ (نھیں) and م+F060+ا → ه (مهارو).",
    "F061 is ه, except before د → ھ (ھُدرو). هوا and هور stay ه."
  ],
